<title>SPAIN: Spain's Santander Q1 attributable up 23.7%.</title>
<headline>Spain's Santander Q1 attributable up 23.7%.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Santander announced on Tuesday following first quarter group results (in billion pesetas, unless stated):</p>
<p>    Attributable net profit	    24.8    vs  20.05</p>
<p>    Net interest income		 116.82   vs  95.37</p>
<p>    Ordinary income		     184.87   vs 145.33</p>
<p>    Operating income		     60.36   vs  41.31</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			  48.50   vs  38.92</p>
<p>    Net profit			     36.37   vs  28.47</p>
<p> Interest income			384.06     vs    372.60</p>
<p> Equity-accounted dividends	   4.87     vs	7.29</p>
<p> Interest expenses		    272.11     vs    284.52</p>
<p> Fees and commissions		  46.81     vs     37.20</p>
<p> Financial/trading income	    21.24     vs     12.76</p>
<p> Operating costs			109.08     vs     91.46</p>
<p>    -personnel costs		   73.70     vs     61.83</p>
<p>    -general, administrative cost  35.38     vs     29.63</p>
<p> Depreciation			    13.24     vs     11.65</p>
<p> Other operating costs		  2.19     vs	0.91</p>
<p>Net earnings from equity-accounted</p>
<p>    holdings			     13.18     vs     23.90</p>
<p>Adjustment for equity-acc.</p>
<p>    dividends			     4.87     vs	7.29</p>
<p> Amortisation of goodwill	     6.00     vs	3.81</p>
<p> Net loan-loss provisions	    11.06     vs     12.14</p>
<p> Writedown of investment securities 0.84     vs	0.13</p>
<p> Net extraordinary gain		 2.30     vs	0.12 loss</p>
<p> Corporate income tax provision    12.13     vs     10.45</p>
<p> Average total assets	    20,531.20     vs 16,943.96</p>
<p> Average Equity			 582.17     vs    536.92</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
